    "Robot, extra object, selected PROS workspace and mode duration differ; observed speed ratios do not isolate the fix. Start pose is unchanged.",
    "The 120 Hz case completes competition sooner; both rates cover different simulation durations and settling phases.",
    "Native step is synchronous CPU work, GPU execution and synchronization together; no kernel occupancy or individual component timing.",
    "Raw contact counts include mirrored/subdivided manifold reports; retained pairs are presence only, not forces or an exact sleep count.",
    "Stage totals cover all ticks; p50/p95 describe only the most recent 2048 completions.",
    "Device-wide GPU telemetry can include other applications; no per-process or CPU-core utilization was captured.",
    "The retained contact-pair gauge is only a final observation, not a per-tick trace.",
    "Stationary rendering capacity is not interactive GUI FPS; the user-reported 80-100% GUI utilization is a separate workload.",
    "GPU claw placement is measured against the prototype contact-based scorer, not an official game-rule acceptance suite."
